/* APEVERSE 2.1 - amsterdam_zuid.js : AMSTERDAM second district — the Museum quarter + Vondelpark (south of the canal ring).
   world_amsterdam.js owns the ground, the Singelgracht canal, its 3 bridges and the pond holes (surface); this file builds the rest
   as its own merged blocks (culled as blocks) and runs its life.  1 m = 1 m, north is -z.  Layout (not a survey of the real city):
     Vijzelstraat (canal-house rows, built by the world file) -> Singelgracht bridges -> Stadhouderskade (road, tram terminus, a row of
     grand houses with brand shops: SWAG, ApePhone, SOLTERRA Living, Chocolaterie Puur, Pannenkoekenhuis De Zuidkant)
     -> the Nationaal Apenmuseum (fictional; a red-brick museum with towers and a public passage you walk through; one gallery
        inside with 9 procedural paintings, ticket desk, museum shop, a gallery trail)
     -> Museumplein (lawn, long pool, ice cream + poffertjes, the Klankgebouw concert hall and Museum Nu: exteriors)
     -> Vondelpark (gate, winding paths, three ponds with ducks, big trees, willows, rose garden, bandstand, Theehuis De Reiger,
        a lawn jam session in the afternoon, bike rental, cyclists, parakeets).
   Residents: Ruben (museum guide), Sanne (park gardener), Lotte (busker).  Every business is fictional.  Save: S.ams (optional fields). */
